      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:9:2:6",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ الصَّادِقَ ( عليه السلام ) مَتَى أَضْرِبُ دَابَّتِي تَحْتِي فَقَالَ إِذَا لَمْ تَمْشِ تَحْتَكَ كَمَشْيَتِهَا إِلَى مِذْوَدِهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ali Bin Ibrahim Al Ja’fary, raising it, said, ",
          "‘I asked Al-Sadiq<sup>asws</sup>, ‘When can I strike my animal under me?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When it does not walk under you like it walks to its feeding place’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Ja‘fariy in a marfu‘ manner has said the following: “I once asked al-Sadiq, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, ‘When can I hit my stumper?’ He (the Imam) said, ‘You can do so when you are riding and it does not walk as it does when going to its manger, its feeding place.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
